            "review_title": "Review at Nha Trang Seafoods",
            "review_text": "AlwaysHungryForLife\nAustralia59 contributions\n0\nCame here following a recommendation\nJan 2020\nCame here following a recommendation from the hotel when we asked for a decent place selling seafood. Menus were available in English and the prices were fair. \n\nWe enjoyed the prawns cooked in butter and garlic, glass noodles with crab, stir fried morning glory. Seafood fried rice tasted good but it would be hard to spot the seafood in it. The grilled fish (pomfret) was the disappointing dish - a bit dry and I don’t think they fully gutted the fish. \n\nThere was a nice selection of fresh seafood (fish, prawns, shell fish, crabs etc) all of which can be selected by yourself and weighed. We kept a photo record of the weight but the bill was accurate. We thought the price of dinner was decent by Aussie standards. \n\nWould recommend\nRead more\nWritten January 2, 2020",
