            "review_title": "Review at Nha Trang Seafoods",
            "review_text": "Annalice C\nMudgee, Australia49 contributions\n0\nPoor service but food was ok\nMay 2019 • Family\nWe went to this restaurant on the recommendation from a tour guide we had. We ordered 3 lobsters (1 grilled and 2 baked) as well as 2 prawn dishes and some steamed rice. \nThey gave us some wet wipes with our drinks which was fine. The 2 prawn dishes came out fine and then there was 1 half lobster baked and 1 half lobster grilled. After trying to explain we wanted 3 whole lobsters, we waited about 20 minutes for our full meal. The lobsters came out on a big plate all together and then we had side plates to eat this off which was somewhat difficult. \n\nWe never ended up with any rice and then they tried to charge us for the wet wipes as “cold towels” on our bill. They apparently cost VND4,000 each, however we did not ask for them and refused to pay for them.\n\nIf you speak Vietnamese well, this restaurant would be ok but they really struggled with English even when we pointed specifically to what we wanted on the menu. \n\nWe paid nearly $200 AUD for this very average meal and a couple of soft drinks. We won’t be back.\nRead more\nWritten May 20, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
