            "review_title": "Review at Nha Trang Seafoods",
            "review_text": "Robbie L\nSydney, Australia6 contributions\n0\nDon’t bother!!\nJul 2018 • Friends\nWe came to this restaurant in a group of ten because our tour guide recommended it, so we thought why not, we were up for a bit of fresh fish on the menu. The staff were quite prompt to accommodate us in combining two tables so we could sit together which was great. Ordering drinks was a different matter. They came by after a spell and took the orders off four of us and not the others. Amazing! We had to keep asking for the waiter to come over so that the others could order their drinks. After some time our warm beers came over, whilst another couple were pointing to their drink orders off the drinks menu, because the staffs English was quite poor. The waitress in the meantime, thought it convenient for her to turn her back on them and rolled her eyes. How bloody rude!! We were all discussed with their attitude and thought that was enough for us. If it was hard enough to get drinks from them, how hard would it be to order the food. We wouldn’t stand for anymore. We asked for the drinks bill so that we could leave. All to our surprise, they added the cost of some packaged face towlets which we didn’t even ask for. I know they are cheap but seriously, everywhere else we have travelled in this beautiful country has never charged us for it. Anyway, we payed them and left, discussed and angry. What a let down. \n Do yourself a favour and don’t give this place any time of day. \n\nRob\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 31, 2018",
